      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, these are getting closer to the vibe. the scores are looking a bit better. \n\nbut i'm seeing a lot of pushback from my lead on the \"tone\" specifically. they're worried the messages still feel too \"heavy\" or \"negative\" because the words 'failed', 'insufficient', or 'low balance' are being flagged by the sentiment tool, which drags the score down.\n\ncan you try one more round? i really need to see those positivity scores climb significantly so we can pass the internal audit. i know i said not to go overboard, but we really need these to feel bright and uplifting to offset the bad news of the transfer failing. i'm looking for a higher tier of optimism, just please... try to keep it even remotely tethered to a banking app. \n\ncan you give me 3 more that maximize that positivity score?",
